\periph Source Statement|id="pubdata"
\mt1 SOURCE STATEMENT
\ip The Old Testament and Apocrypha are eBible.org’s transcription of Sir Lancelot Charles Lee Brenton’s English Septuagint, with documented corrections to the 1870 text. The historical introductions, abbreviations, notes, and appendices are retained. The source’s Errata describes its editorial corrections; this volume is not a facsimile.
\ip The New Testament contains the 27 books of eBible.org’s KJV Cambridge Paragraph Bible (engkjvcpb). The Epistle Dedicatory follows Brenton’s 1870 introduction, then The Translators to the Reader. Closing notes remain with their NT books. The historical Cambridge title page is omitted. Scrivener’s critical introduction and scholarly appendices are absent from the digital package. Both source distributions identify their texts as public domain. eBible’s KJV notice records the continuing Crown printing rights in the United Kingdom.
\ip Source snapshots retrieved 23 September 2026 from eBible.org: eng-Brenton_usfm.zip and engkjvcpb_usfm.zip. Exact checksums and the reproducible build configuration accompany this edition.
\ip Combined Ezra–Nehemiah retains its 23 chapters. The overlapping standalone Nehemiah file is excluded. Esther and Daniel include their embedded additions. Psalm 151, Prayer of Manasses, and 3–4 Maccabees are retained. No 2 Esdras is included.
\ip The source wording, verse labels, added-word italics, notes, and references have been retained. The book order, title pages, section dividers, and contents belong to this edition. Historical opinions in the apparatus belong to their original authors.
\ip Typeset with PTXprint 3.0.43, using its BSB A5 layout, Charis, Gentium Plus for Greek quotations, and Ezra SIL for Hebrew quotations. This is an English Bible; original-language passages occur only within the historical apparatus and notes.
